[
    {
        "content": "<p>A short question, but is there any reason not to have <code>volume.comap NNReal.toReal</code> as the <code>volume</code> on <code>NNReal</code>? I looked for previous discussions here but could not find any.</p>",
        "id": 605826407,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1782154341
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I see no reason not to</p>",
        "id": 605837512,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1782156852
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you're adding that you could also add a <code>MeasureSpace (Subtype p)</code> instance to match <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Subtype.instMeasurableSpace#doc\">docs#Subtype.instMeasurableSpace</a>.<br>\nIt's also strange that we have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MeasurableSpace.comap#doc\">docs#MeasurableSpace.comap</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MeasureTheory.Measure.comap#doc\">docs#MeasureTheory.Measure.comap</a> but no <code>MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace.comap</code></p>",
        "id": 605837776,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1782156912
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I also wondered about subtypes. I think sometimes comap would not the measure we want, but in that case it could be wrapped in a <code>def</code></p>",
        "id": 605844051,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1782158450
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think we want this in Mathlib.<br>\nNote that this already exists in the Carleson project (and is probably ready for upstreaming):<br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/fpvandoorn/carleson/blob/master/Carleson/ToMathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/NNReal.lean\">https://github.com/fpvandoorn/carleson/blob/master/Carleson/ToMathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/NNReal.lean</a></p>\n<p>At first I was hesitant about adding these instances, but <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"726665\">@Leo Diedering</span> convinced me that this is (sometimes) useful.</p>",
        "id": 605848320,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1782159483
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"933054\">Snir Broshi</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/volume.20on.20.E2.84.9D.E2.89.A50/near/605837776\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If you're adding that you could also add a <code>MeasureSpace (Subtype p)</code> instance to match <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Subtype.instMeasurableSpace#doc\">docs#Subtype.instMeasurableSpace</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>No, we don't want that. Think of a line inside a two-dimensional space: we don't want to put the restriction of the two-dimensional measure (which would just be zero) but instead the one-dimensional measure.</p>",
        "id": 605853132,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1782160493
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's also not <em>that</em> natural in that if your <code>Subtype p</code> is a non-nullmeasurable set, then you get the zero measure as <code>comap</code></p>",
        "id": 605853929,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1782160666
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"933054\">Snir Broshi</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/volume.20on.20.E2.84.9D.E2.89.A50/near/605837776\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It's also strange that we have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MeasurableSpace.comap#doc\">docs#MeasurableSpace.comap</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MeasureTheory.Measure.comap#doc\">docs#MeasureTheory.Measure.comap</a> but no <code>MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace.comap</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This seems like a pretty safe idea at least</p>",
        "id": 605854247,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1782160734
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think Sébastien's example also suggests that we don't want <code>MeasureSpace.comap</code>.</p>",
        "id": 605869666,
        "sender_full_name": "Yongxi Lin (Aaron)",
        "timestamp": 1782165937
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think it does not cost anything to have the definition to use it to define specific instances.</p>",
        "id": 605869813,
        "sender_full_name": "Etienne Marion",
        "timestamp": 1782166009
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The <code>comap</code> definition also seems weaker than it should be. The restriction of the outer measure to <code>MeasurableSpace.comap</code> is always a measure, even if some sets map to non-measurable sets. I have seen this construction being used to give an example of a measure-preserving system that does not have an invertible extension.</p>",
        "id": 605873119,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1782167908
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MeasureTheory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Classical</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">comap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hβ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MeasurableSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">μ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Measure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Measure</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hβ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Injective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">OuterMeasure</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">μ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toOuterMeasure</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toMeasure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ms</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hβ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MeasurableSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">measurableSet_comap</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hs</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">rcases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">hu</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">OuterMeasure</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comap_apply</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">image_inter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">image_sdiff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">image_preimage_eq_range_inter</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sdiff_inter</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inter_assoc</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">inter_eq_self_of_subset_left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">image_subset_range</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">..</span><span class=\"o\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">sdiff_eq_empty</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">image_subset_range</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">..</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">empty_union</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">measure_inter_add_sdiff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hu</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 605877436,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1782170726
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110050\">Sébastien Gouëzel</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/volume.20on.20.E2.84.9D.E2.89.A50/near/605853132\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>No, we don't want that. Think of a line inside a two-dimensional space: we don't want to put the restriction of the two-dimensional measure (which would just be zero) but instead the one-dimensional measure.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>If we follow this logic, shouldn't the existing <code>MeasurableSpace</code> instance be removed as well? If you took such a line inside the two-dimensional space with the <code>NullMeasurable</code> algebra, then the algebra on the subspace would not make any sense either.</p>",
        "id": 605930660,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1782200534
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that Mathlib convention is to <em>never</em> complete the sigma-algebra. Hence <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Subtype.instMeasurableSpace#doc\">docs#Subtype.instMeasurableSpace</a> seems completely reasonable to me.</p>",
        "id": 605937299,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1782202477
    }
]